    "responses": [
      {
        "turn": 1,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Hi! I\u2019m interested in finding a good shampoo. Any suggestions?",
          "user_rubrik": "What is a good shampoo for my hair?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "If you're looking for a good shampoo, especially considering your frequent use of heat styling tools, I recommend trying a sulfate-free moisturizing shampoo. Some great options include:\n\n1. **Amika The Kure Repair Shampoo** - This shampoo contains hydrolyzed keratin and avocado oil, which can help restore damaged hair and fight frizz.\n2. **Pureology Strength Cure Shampoo** - Ideal for colored or chemically treated hair, this sulfate-free shampoo strengthens and smooths your hair while maintaining vibrancy.\n3. **L'Or\u00e9al Paris Elvive Dream Lengths Restoring Shampoo** - A budget-friendly option that helps seal split ends and strengthen long hair.\n4. **SheaMoisture Raw Shea Butter Moisture Retention Shampoo** - This creamy formula provides plenty of moisture and is great for reviving damaged strands.\n\nAdditionally, consider incorporating a deep conditioning treatment once a week to keep your hair hydrated and healthy.",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0012-59-02864:1": 1.2883031368255615,
            "clueweb22-en0007-83-07134:12": 1.171985387802124,
            "clueweb22-en0018-17-18656:3": 0.9840025305747986,
            "clueweb22-en0038-80-07080:4": 0.6351003646850586,
            "clueweb22-en0003-05-15895:6": 0.3475796580314636,
            "clueweb22-en0038-80-07080:6": 0.2354036122560501,
            "clueweb22-en0001-52-06865:21": 0.2189396768808365,
            "clueweb22-en0034-34-08785:1": 0.2134685516357422,
            "clueweb22-en0007-10-18814:7": 0.014072433114051819
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": [
            "I frequently use heat styling tools to keep my hair looking good;",
            "I'm allergic to nuts, so I have to be careful about ingredients;"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 2,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Thanks! What ingredients in the shampoo should I look out for?",
          "user_rubrik": "What ingredients in the shampoo i should look out for?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "When choosing a shampoo, especially considering your heat styling routine, look for the following beneficial ingredients:\n\n1. **Sulfate-free formulas**: These are gentler on your hair and help retain moisture.\n2. **Natural oils**: Ingredients like coconut oil, argan oil, and olive oil nourish and hydrate your hair.\n3. **Keratin**: This protein helps repair damaged hair and protects against heat.\n4. **Humectants**: Glycerin and panthenol are great for moisture retention and fortifying hair.\n5. **Butters**: Shea butter and mango butter provide intense hydration and form a protective layer.\n6. **Vitamins**: Look for Vitamin E and B5, which nourish and strengthen hair.\n\nAvoid harsh ingredients like sulfates, isopropyl alcohol, and formaldehyde, as they can dry out your hair and cause damage.",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0007-83-07134:12": 2.12540340423584,
            "clueweb22-en0012-19-10758:21": 1.798855185508728,
            "clueweb22-en0012-59-02864:1": 1.31781005859375,
