    "responses": [
      {
        "turn": 1,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "I\u2019m looking for advice on a good shampoo. My scalp and hair tend to get oily, so I need something that can help with that. Any recommendations?",
          "user_rubrik": "What is a good shampoo for my hair?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Here are some great shampoo recommendations for oily hair that can help you manage excess oil and keep your scalp feeling fresh:\n\n1. **Verb Ghost Shampoo** - A gentle option that uses moringa seed oil for frizz control and contains sunflower seed extract for UV protection. It also has a light, fresh fragrance.\n\n2. **Paul Mitchell Tea Tree Special Shampoo** - This shampoo features tea tree oil, which effectively cleanses impurities from your hair and scalp, leaving it lustrous and invigorated with peppermint and lavender.\n\n3. **Neutrogena T/Sal Therapeutic Shampoo** - Contains salicylic acid, which is well-regarded for breaking down oil and preventing buildup.\n\n4. **Aveda Scalp Benefits Balancing Shampoo** - Formulated with echinacea and sage to refresh your scalp and clear away dead skin cells.\n\n5. **Klorane Shampoo with Nettle** - Naturally balances oil production and helps you extend the time between washes.\n\n6. **R+Co Oblivion Clarifying Shampoo** - A cult classic that gently cleanses away product buildup and pollution without stripping moisture.\n\n7. **Silkpro Hairgro Shampoo for Oily Scalp** - Claims to improve scalp condition",
          "citations": {
