    "responses": [
      {
        "turn": 6,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Thanks! I\u2019ve heard of OUAI and Head & Shoulders\u2014how do those brands compare for oily scalp and hair?",
          "user_rubrik": "Tell me more about OUAI and Head and Shoulders brands for shampoo for oily scalp and hair.\u00a0",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Both OUAI and Head & Shoulders offer products that cater to oily hair, but they have different focuses and formulations. \n\n**OUAI** is known for its high-quality, salon-inspired products that often include nourishing ingredients. Their shampoos, like the **OUAI Detox Shampoo**, are designed to remove buildup and excess oil while being gentle on the hair and scalp. OUAI products typically have a more luxurious feel and are focused on overall hair health.\n\n**Head & Shoulders**, on the other hand, specializes in anti-dandruff solutions. Their shampoos, such as the **Head & Shoulders Instant Oil Control Shampoo**, are specifically formulated to target dandruff and oily scalps. They contain active ingredients like pyrithione zinc, which helps to reduce flaking and control oiliness effectively.\n\nIf your primary concern is managing oiliness and dandruff, Head & Shoulders might be the better option. However, if you're looking for a more holistic approach to hair care with a focus on nourishment and styling, OUAI could be a great choice.",
          "citations": {
