    "responses": [
      {
        "turn": 1,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "I\u2019m trying to find a good shampoo for my hair. Any recommendations?",
          "user_rubrik": "What is a good shampoo for my hair?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Since you frequently use heat styling tools, it's important to choose a shampoo that protects against heat damage and keeps your hair hydrated. Look for shampoos specifically designed for heat-styled hair, such as those with keratin or moisturizing ingredients like coconut oil or almond oil. For example, L\u2019Or\u00e9al Paris Smooth Intense Ultimate Straight Shampoo is formulated to protect against heat up to 450 degrees and can help reduce damage from styling tools. Additionally, using a heat protectant spray or balm alongside your shampoo can further shield your hair from damage. Avoid shampoos with harsh sulfates, as they can strip your hair of natural oils, leaving it dry and brittle.",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0015-92-16806:7": 19.69179916381836,
            "clueweb22-en0021-78-06954:13": 19.608200073242188,
            "clueweb22-en0039-71-11631:17": 19.17009925842285
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": [
            "I frequently use heat styling tools to keep my hair looking good."
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 2,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That\u2019s helpful! Are there any ingredients in shampoo I should avoid, especially considering I have an oily scalp and I\u2019m allergic to nuts?",
          "user_rubrik": "What ingredients in the shampoo i should look out for?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "To address your oily scalp and nut allergy, avoid shampoos containing nut-derived oils like almond or macadamia oil. Instead, opt for sulfate-free shampoos, as sulfates can irritate the scalp and exacerbate oiliness. Ingredients like witch hazel and celery seed extract can help balance sebum production, while tea tree oil and rosemary oil are excellent for cleansing and soothing the scalp. Additionally, steer clear of heavily fragranced shampoos, as they often contain chemicals that might irritate sensitive skin. A product like Maple Holistics Degrease Shampoo, which is sulfate-free and uses natural ingredients, could be a good fit for your needs.",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0010-88-09918:1": 24.131200790405273,
            "clueweb22-en0041-54-13093:6": 22.89240074157715,
            "clueweb22-en0016-35-00824:4": 22.45509910583496
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": [
            "I'm allergic to nuts, so I have to be careful about ingredients."
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 3,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Thanks for the tips! Any drugstore shampoos you'd recommend for oily scalp, maybe something I can find easily?",
          "user_rubrik": "What shampoos exist for an oily scalp and hair?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "For a drugstore shampoo that suits your oily scalp and avoids nut-derived ingredients, consider L\u2019Or\u00e9al Paris Elvive Extraordinary Clay Rebalancing Shampoo. It\u2019s designed to balance oil production and is widely available. Another option is Neutrogena Exfoliating Healthy Scalp Clarify & Shine Shampoo, which is pH-balanced and free of parabens and phthalates, making it gentle yet effective for oily hair. Both are affordable and easy to find in most stores or online.",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0009-90-06329:0": 23.66939926147461,
            "clueweb22-en0038-99-06448:0": 22.059200286865234
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": [
            "I'm allergic to nuts, so I have to be careful about ingredients."
          ]
        }
