          "user_utterance": "Thanks! What ingredients in the shampoo should I look out for? Especially with my allergies and oily scalp.",
          "user_rubrik": "What ingredients in the shampoo i should look out for?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Given your nut allergy, it's important to avoid shampoos containing nut-derived oils such as almond, argan, or macadamia oils, as these can trigger allergic reactions. For an oily scalp, look for shampoos with clarifying ingredients like tea tree oil, rosemary, lemon, or cypress, which help regulate sebum production and keep your scalp balanced [DOC-1][DOC-2]. Sulfate-free shampoos are recommended, as sulfates can irritate sensitive skin and potentially worsen allergies [DOC-4]. Hypoallergenic shampoos with minimal ingredients, and without added fragrances or dyes, are also a safer choice for those with allergies [DOC-3]. Always check ingredient lists carefully and opt for products labeled as hypoallergenic or formulated for sensitive skin. Would you like specific product recommendations that meet these criteria?",
