    "responses": [
      {
        "turn": 4,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That\u2019s helpful! I\u2019ve seen OUAI and Head & Shoulders recommended, too. How do those brands compare for oily scalp and hair?",
          "user_rubrik": "Tell me more about OUAI and Head and Shoulders brands for shampoo for oily scalp and hair.\u00a0",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Head & Shoulders has a range of shampoos for different scalp types, including the Instant Oil Control Shampoo, which is formulated to deeply cleanse and control excess oil on the scalp and hair, making it a strong choice for oily scalps [DOC-4]. However, some Head & Shoulders variants, such as the Dry Scalp Care with Almond Oil, contain nut-derived ingredients, so you should avoid those and always check the label for nut oils [DOC-2]. The active ingredient in most Head & Shoulders shampoos is zinc pyrithione, which helps with dandruff and oil control, and the brand is generally considered gentle for regular use [DOC-1][DOC-3]. OUAI is also recommended for oily hair, but many of their products contain nut oils (like almond or macadamia), which are not suitable for those with nut allergies. Therefore, for oily scalps and nut allergies, Head & Shoulders Instant Oil Control is a safer and effective option, provided you avoid formulas with nut oils. Do you want tips on how often to wash oily hair?",
