          "user_utterance": "Hi! I\u2019m looking for some advice about shampoos\u2014what\u2019s a good option for my hair, especially if my scalp tends to get oily?",
          "user_rubrik": "What is a good shampoo for my hair?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "For your oily scalp, especially since you frequently use heat styling tools and have sensitive skin, shampoos with clarifying essential oils such as lemon, rosemary, and cypress are highly recommended. These ingredients help regulate excess sebum, minimize pore size, and promote scalp health without over-drying. Many of these shampoos are sulfate- and paraben-free, making them suitable for sensitive skin and color-treated hair. Options like natural clarifying shampoos with jojoba and botanical keratin are also gentle and effective, and some formulas specifically mention being safe for those with allergies and sensitive skin. Always check the ingredient list to ensure the product is nut-free, given your allergy. Brands like Dr Groot and Moist Diane Botanical offer gentle, daily-use shampoos that cleanse and nourish the scalp, helping to control oil and support hair health, which is ideal for your needs as a 40-year-old woman who heat styles regularly and values minimal downtime in your routine [DOC-1][DOC-4]. Would you like specific product recommendations that are nut-free?",
