          "text": "The best ingredients for shampoos targeting oily scalps include tea tree oil, which helps remove impurities and balance oil production, as well as peppermint and rosemary for their scalp-invigorating and oil-controlling properties. Lemon and clary sage are also beneficial for balancing sebum. Sulfate-free formulas are recommended to avoid over-stripping, which can trigger more oil production. Avoid heavy oils (like argan or jojoba, especially given your nut allergy) and synthetic fragrances. Shampoos such as Paul Mitchell Tea Tree Special Shampoo and formulas with natural botanical ingredients (like Seed Phytonutrients Daily Hair Cleanser) are good options for frequent use and maintaining scalp health without causing irritation or excess oiliness [DOC-1][DOC-2][DOC-3][DOC-4]. Are you interested in tips for managing oily hair between washes?",
