          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Yes, please! Can you share some tips for extending time between washes when you have an oily scalp?",
          "user_rubrik": "What shampoos exist for an oily scalp and hair?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "To manage an oily scalp and go longer between washes, try using a dry shampoo to absorb excess oil at the roots. Avoid applying heavy conditioners or styling products directly to your scalp, as these can increase oiliness. Opt for shampoos labeled 'volumizing,' 'strengthening,' or 'balancing,' and avoid those marketed as 'moisturizing' or 'hydrating,' which may be too rich for your scalp type. Washing your hair every other day or 2-3 times a week is ideal; over-washing can actually trigger more oil production. Silicone-free products are also recommended, as silicones can build up and make hair look greasier. If you work out frequently, rinse your hair with water or use a gentle, nut-free dry shampoo between washes to refresh your scalp without stripping it [DOC-1][DOC-2][DOC-3]. Would you like recommendations for nut-free dry shampoos?",
