          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "OUAI shampoos, including their Super Dry Shampoo, are formulated to cleanse, remove buildup, and add volume to fine, oily hair without parabens or sulfates, making them suitable for frequent use and sensitive scalps. Their products are designed to be user-friendly and are generally considered safe for those with ingredient sensitivities, but you should always check for nut-derived oils in specific formulas [DOC-1][DOC-14]. Head & Shoulders, on the other hand, is primarily known for its anti-dandruff properties due to the active ingredient Zinc Pyrithione, which also helps reduce scalp inflammation and can be beneficial for oily scalps. They offer a range of formulas, so choosing one labeled for oily hair or scalp is important. Both brands have options for oily scalps, but OUAI focuses more on gentle cleansing and volume, while Head & Shoulders targets dandruff and scalp health [DOC-11]. Always review ingredient lists for nut-derived components to ensure safety. Would you like specific nut-free product recommendations from either brand?",
