          "text": "For oily hair\u2014especially with frequent heat styling and a nut allergy\u2014choose a shampoo that is:\n\n- **Clarifying but gentle**: Removes oil and buildup without stripping or drying, which is crucial for heat-styled hair.\n- **Nut oil-free**: Avoid products with argan, almond, macadamia, or similar oils.\n- **Protective and strengthening**: Look for ingredients that support hair health under heat.\n\n**Top Recommendations:**\n\n**1. Maple Holistics Degrease Shampoo**\n- **Why:** Sulfate-free, clarifying, and formulated with lemon, rosemary, and cypress oils (no nut oils). Designed for oily scalps and safe for color/heat-styled hair.\n- **Bonus:** Plant-based, paraben-free, and suitable for sensitive skin.\n\n**2. Paul Mitchell Tea Tree Special Shampoo**\n- **Why:** Deep cleanses with tea tree, peppermint, and lavender oils (no nut oils). Antimicrobial, helps with oil and scalp health, and invigorates hair.\n- **Heat Styling:** Leaves hair bouncy,",
