          "user_rubrik_score": 3,
          "text": "For oily hair\u2014especially with frequent heat styling and a nut allergy\u2014the best treatments are those that control oil, protect from heat, and avoid nut-derived ingredients.\n\n**Top Treatment Strategies:**\n\n- **Weekly Clarifying Mask:** Use a clay-based or charcoal mask (no nut oils) once a week to deeply cleanse the scalp and absorb excess oil. Avoid heavy, oil-based masks.\n- **Lightweight, Oil-Free Conditioners:** Apply only to mid-lengths and ends, never the roots, to avoid extra oiliness.\n- **Heat Protection:** Always use a nut-free heat protectant spray before styling. Look for products labeled \u201coil-free\u201d or those using ingredients like silicones (e.g., dimethicone, cyclopentasiloxane) rather than argan, almond, or macadamia oils.\n- **Essential Oils for Scalp Balance:** Tea tree, rosemary, lemon, and lemongrass oils can help regulate oil production\u2014ensure the product is nut-free.\n- **Professional Hair Spa Treatments:** Ask for oil-control formulas at salons; these can normalize scalp",
