          "user_rubrik_score": 2,
          "text": "Essential oils can be highly effective for oily hair\u2014especially when you need to avoid nut-derived ingredients and protect against heat styling.\n\n**Best Essential Oils for Oily Hair (Nut-Free):**\n- **Tea Tree, Lemon, Rosemary, Lemongrass, Sage, Cedarwood, Cypress, Ylang-Ylang**\n  - These oils help regulate scalp oil production, clarify, and have antimicrobial properties. Multiple sources confirm their use in both shampoos and DIY treatments for oily hair.\n\n**Safety & Usage:**\n- **Generally Safe** when diluted properly (in water, aloe vera gel, or a non-nut carrier like grapeseed or jojoba oil\u2014verify the source of jojoba if you have severe allergies).\n- **Patch Test First:** Essential oils are potent and can cause irritation or allergic reactions. Always test a small amount on your skin before applying to your scalp.\n- **Avoid Nut Oils:** Do not use essential oils diluted in almond, argan, macadamia, or other nut oils.\n\n**How to Use:**\n- Add a few drops to your shampoo or",
