          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "What about the difference between rinse-out and leave-in conditioners for oily hair?",
          "user_rubrik": "What does Head and Shoulders, OUAI and La Roche-Posay shampoos cost?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 0,
          "text": "For oily, heat-styled, nut-allergic hair, here\u2019s what matters when choosing between rinse-out and leave-in conditioners:\n\n**Rinse-Out Conditioners**\n- **Best for oily hair:** They hydrate and detangle without lingering residue, which is crucial since leave-behind oils can worsen greasiness (clueweb22-en0036-12-09383, clueweb22-en0002-56-18071).\n- **How to use:** Apply only to mid-lengths and ends, never the scalp. Rinse thoroughly to avoid buildup, flatness, or clogged pores\u2014especially important for oily scalps.\n- **Nut-free:** Always check labels for nut oils or extracts.\n\n**Leave-In Conditioners**\n- **Lighter, but riskier for oily hair:** Designed to be left in, they\u2019re typically lightweight, but even these can weigh down fine or oily hair if overused (clueweb22-en0015-02-03641, clueweb22-en0035-08-00598).\n- **Best use:** Occasional application to ends",
