      {
        "turn": 11,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "What are some common mistakes people make with their haircare routines?",
          "user_rubrik": "What does Head and Shoulders, OUAI and La Roche-Posay shampoos cost?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 0,
          "text": "Absolutely\u2014here are the most common mistakes people make with haircare routines, especially for oily, heat-styled, and nut-allergic hair:\n\n**1. Overwashing or Underwashing**\n- Washing too often can strip natural oils, causing your scalp to overproduce sebum (clueweb22-en0001-52-06865). But not washing enough leads to buildup from oil, sweat, and styling products (clueweb22-en0036-34-04746). Find your balance\u2014usually every day or every other day for oily hair.\n\n**2. Applying Conditioner to the Scalp**\n- Conditioner on roots can make hair limp and greasy. Always apply only to mid-lengths and ends (clueweb22-en0009-62-00433).\n\n**3. Using Heavy or Oily Products**\n- Heavy creams, oils, and silicone-based products can weigh hair down and worsen oiliness (clueweb22-en0044-18-15248, clueweb22-en0016-35-00824). Stick to lightweight, oil-free, and silicone",
