      {
        "turn": 2,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Sounds great, any specific ingredients to avoid in shampoos?",
          "user_rubrik": "What ingredients in the shampoo i should look out for?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "For oily hair\u2014especially with frequent heat styling and a nut allergy\u2014avoid shampoos containing:\n\n**1. Sulfates:**  \n- Sodium Lauryl Sulfate (SLS), Sodium Laureth Sulfate (SLES), Ammonium Laureth Sulfate  \n  *Why avoid?* These harsh detergents strip natural oils, causing dryness, irritation, and potential long-term damage\u2014especially risky with heat styling.\n\n**2. Nut Oils and Extracts:**  \n- Argan, almond, macadamia, shea, and other tree nut derivatives  \n  *Why avoid?* Even topical exposure can trigger allergic reactions.\n\n**3. Harsh Alcohols:**  \n- Denatured alcohol, isopropyl alcohol  \n  *Why avoid?* These dry out hair and scalp, compounding heat damage.\n\n**4. DEA/MEA/TEA Compounds:**  \n- Cocamide DEA, Lauramide DEA, Triethanolamine  \n  *Why avoid?* Linked to skin irritation and potential carcinogenic risks.\n\n**5. Sodium Chloride:**",
