          "user_utterance": "Any tips for choosing the right conditioner for oily hair?",
          "user_rubrik": "What does Head and Shoulders, OUAI and La Roche-Posay shampoos cost?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 0,
          "text": "For oily hair that\u2019s frequently heat-styled and nut-allergic, the right conditioner is crucial for balancing moisture without adding grease or triggering allergies.\n\n**What to Look For:**\n- **Lightweight, oil-free formulas:** Prevents hair from feeling heavy or greasy (clueweb22-en0042-65-10707, clueweb22-en0011-94-06370).\n- **Apply only to mid-lengths and ends:** Never on the scalp or roots\u2014this avoids extra oiliness (clueweb22-en0034-28-19815, clueweb22-en0007-71-14163, clueweb22-en0011-69-17278).\n- **Nut-free ingredients:** Avoid conditioners with argan, almond, macadamia, shea, or other nut oils (your allergy constraint).\n- **Heat protection:** Some conditioners offer thermal protection\u2014ideal for frequent styling (clueweb22-en0015-92-16806).\n\n**Recommended Types/Brands:**\n- **Paul Mitchell Tea Tree Special Conditioner:** Lightweight, clarifying,",
