          "text": "For oily hair and scalp, consider a gentle, sulfate-free shampoo that deeply cleans both the scalp and hair. Look for a product containing natural ingredients like peppermint oil, eucalyptus oil, or panthenol, which can help control oil production and improve scalp circulation. Some shampoos are specifically formulated to purify and balance the scalp, leaving your hair shiny but not oily. You may also want to try washing your hair more frequently, at least four times a week, to remove excess oils. Avoid using heavy, oily styling products and consider a dry shampoo to absorb excess oil between washes.",
