          "text": "When choosing a shampoo, it's best to avoid ingredients like sulfates, such as sodium lauryl sulfate, sodium laureth sulfate, or ammonium lauryl sulfate, as they can strip your hair of its natural moisture and cause dryness. Additionally, be cautious of parabens, phthalates, and formaldehyde, which can have negative effects on your hair and overall health. Opt for natural ingredients like essential oils, coconut oil, or olive oil, which can help nourish and protect your hair. If you have specific concerns, such as color-treated hair, you may also want to avoid certain ingredients that can cause color to fade. Always read the ingredient list carefully and look for gentle, sulfate-free options.",
