          "user_utterance": "What are some specific ingredients in shampoos that should be avoided if you have an oily scalp?",
          "user_rubrik": "What ingredients in the shampoo i should look out for?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "If you have an oily scalp, you may want to avoid shampoos that contain ingredients like Sodium Lauryl Sulfate (SLS) and Sodium Laureth Sulfate (SLES), as they can strip the scalp of its natural oils and exacerbate oiliness. You may also want to avoid shampoos that contain propylene glycol, as it can be drying and irritating to the scalp. Additionally, parabens are another ingredient to watch out for, as they can disrupt the balance of the scalp's natural oil production. Look for shampoos that are labeled as \"oil-control\" or \"scalp-soothing\" and contain ingredients like tea tree oil, which can help to balance the scalp's natural oil production and reduce oiliness. It's also a good idea to read reviews and do a patch test before using a new shampoo to ensure that it doesn't irritate your scalp. Get a shampoo that is gentle and suitable for your hair type. Avoid",
