          "user_utterance": "can make your hair greasier. Try to stay away from coconut oil, argan oil, shea butter, and creamy, ultra-hydrating formulas. Sulfate-free shampoos are popular, but some gentle sulfates may actually help lift excess oil if your scalp gets oily fast. Watch for heavy silicones like dimethicone\u2014they can weigh hair down and clog scalp pores. Also, shampoos with a lot of fragrance or artificial color might irritate your scalp, so milder formulas are usually better. Do you have sensitivities or allergies to any ingredients?",
