      {
        "turn": 2,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "What other ingredients should I be careful about in shampoo, especially since I have an oily scalp and sometimes get irritation?",
          "user_rubrik": "What ingredients in the shampoo i should look out for?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "For an oily and irritated scalp, it's best to avoid shampoos containing harsh detergents, fragrances, dyes, and chemicals. Specifically, look out for Sodium Lauryl Sulphate (SLS), as it can be irritating and drying. Many shampoos also highlight being paraben and sulfate-free, indicating these are often best avoided for sensitive scalps. While beneficial for many, some natural ingredients like tea tree oil or rosemary oil can cause irritation for certain individuals, so it's wise to test new products.",
          "citations": {
