        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Got it! I\u2019m allergic to nuts, so I guess I need to be careful about oils too? Are nut oils common in these shampoos?",
          "user_rubrik": "What shampoos exist for an oily scalp and hair?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 0,
          "text": "Yes, nut oils like almond oil and argan (Moroccan) oil are commonly found in shampoos, including some recommended for oily hair. Given your nut allergy, it's crucial to check ingredient lists carefully and avoid products containing oils derived from tree nuts such as sweet almond, argan, or apricot kernel oil. Always consult your allergist about using products with potential allergens.",
