          "user_rubrik": "What ingredients in the shampoo i should look out for?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "For shampoos designed to protect against or repair heat damage from frequent heat styling, look for moisturizing and strengthening ingredients. Key beneficial ingredients include **argan oil, coconut oil, shea butter, keratin, biotin, Pro-Vitamin B5, hydrolyzed silk protein, soy protein, wheat protein, vitamin E, and hyaluronic acid**. These help hydrate, strengthen, and protect your hair.\n\nIt's also generally recommended to **avoid harsh chemicals like sulfates, parabens, and certain drying alcohols** (e.g., cetearyl, cetyl, stearyl alcohol) as they can further strip moisture from damaged hair.",
