      {
        "turn": 3,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Thanks, that\u2019s really helpful! Could using shampoo too often make my scalp oilier?",
          "user_rubrik": "What shampoos exist for an oily scalp and hair?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 0,
          "text": "Yes, using shampoo too often can make your scalp oilier. Frequent washing strips your scalp of its natural oils, prompting your sebaceous glands to produce more sebum to compensate. This can lead to an overproduction of oil and an oilier scalp. For oily hair, it's often recommended to wash every 2-3 days.",
