        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Interesting! Are there any ingredients I should avoid in shampoos, especially for oily hair?",
          "user_rubrik": "What ingredients in the shampoo i should look out for?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "For oily hair and scalp, you should avoid shampoos containing SLS (Sodium Lauryl Sulfate), irritants like diethanolamine (DEA), triethanolamine (TEA), FD&C, D&C, and propylene glycol. Also, steer clear of shampoos with high alcohol content (if it's among the first four ingredients), preservatives like formaldehyde and parabens, and added oils such as mineral oils, petroleum, and lanolin, as these can suffocate hair follicles.",
