    "responses": [
      {
        "turn": 1,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "I\u2019m looking for a good shampoo for my hair. Can you recommend something?",
          "user_rubrik": "What is a good shampoo for my hair?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "happy to help! since you use heat tools and have a nut allergy, i \u2019 ll steer clear of formulas with argan, shea, macadamia, or almond oils. great options : - l \u2019 oreal paris everpure ( moisture or everstrong ) : sulfate - free, color - safe, gentle, and strengthening without nut oils. - pantene pro - v rose water sulfate - free kit : lightweight hydration, paraben - and dye - free, no nut oils. - wow apple cider vinegar shampoo : clarifies buildup from styling ; use 1 \u2013 2x / week and pair with a conditioner you tolerate. tips : - wash 2 \u2013 4x / week ; rotate a clarifying wash ( like the acv ) when hair feels coated. - always use a heat protectant before styling \u2014 want recs without nut oils? - check labels for \u201c argania spinosa kernel oil, \u201d \u201c butyrospermum parkii ( shea ) butter, \u201d macadamia, or almond oils. tell me your hair type ( fine, medium, coarse ), scalp ( dry / oily / sensitive ), and if it \u2019 s color - treated or you prefer",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0023-13-08416:0": 0.4113283157348633,
            "clueweb22-en0042-30-01430:0": -0.09915544837713242,
            "clueweb22-en0009-64-08287:0": -0.22785235941410065,
            "clueweb22-en0004-54-02615:0": -0.579389214515686,
            "clueweb22-en0037-96-04829:3": -0.7622082233428955
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": []
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 2,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That\u2019s super helpful, thank you! What other ingredients should I keep an eye on in shampoo, especially for oily scalp and hair? Also, I\u2019m curious if there are any ingredients to avoid if I want less buildup or irritation.",
          "user_rubrik": "What ingredients in the shampoo i should look out for?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "great question. for an oily scalp / hair, look for : - scalp \u2011 clarifiers : salicylic acid ( bha ), zinc pca, niacinamide. - effective but mild cleansers : sodium laureth sulfate ( sles ), sodium c14 \u2011 16 olefin sulfonate, disodium laureth sulfosuccinate. - degreasing / refreshing add \u2011 ons : tea tree, rosemary, peppermint, eucalyptus, lemon ; apple cider vinegar ; charcoal or clays ( kaolin / bentonite ). - chelators to reduce hard \u2011 water buildup : disodium edta, tetrasodium edta, citric acid. - ph \u2011 balanced formulas ( around 4. 5 \u2013 5. 5 ). to minimize buildup : - limit heavy silicones ( dimethicone, amodimethicone ; choose water \u2011 soluble ones like peg \u2011 8 dimethicone ). - avoid heavy conditioning polymers ( polyquaternium \u2011 10 / 7, quaternium \u2011 80 ) on the scalp. - skip heavy oils / butters on scalp : argan, shea, macadamia, almond,",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0025-02-03737:0": -0.5961459279060364,
            "clueweb22-en0040-70-11805:2": -1.4187641143798828,
            "clueweb22-en0040-70-11805:1": -1.4514409303665161,
            "clueweb22-en0042-31-02488:2": -1.700981616973877,
            "clueweb22-en0018-49-07766:7": -1.9723557233810425
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": []
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 3,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That\u2019s great to know! What about sulfates\u2014are they okay for oily scalps, or should I still avoid them? Also, does washing every day help control the oil, or does it make things worse?",
          "user_rubrik": "What shampoos exist for an oily scalp and hair?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 3,
          "text": "short answer : - sulfates : useful for oily scalps in moderation, but choose gentler ones and don \u2019 t rely on them daily. - daily washing : fine if you use a mild, ph - balanced cleanser ; harsh washes can trigger more oil. details : - strong sulfates like sls are very effective but can over - strip, causing irritation and rebound oil. if you want a sulfate, sles is gentler. many \u201c sulfate - free but strong \u201d options ( olefin sulfonate, sulfosuccinate, betaines ) cleanse oil well without sls / sles. - if your scalp is very oily, daily washing can help and won \u2019 t worsen oil if the formula is gentle ( ph ~ 4. 5 \u2013 5. 5 ). if you ever feel tightness or itch, reduce frequency to every other day. - plan : gentle daily ( or every other day ) scalp - only wash ; condition mid - lengths / ends. use a clarifying wash 1 \u2013 2x / week with salicylic acid, tea tree, or acv to manage buildup from heat styling. - to reduce irritation / buildup : avoid heavy silicones on",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0001-26-09390:1": -2.047065258026123,
            "clueweb22-en0038-27-08700:5": -2.1519663333892822,
            "clueweb22-en0023-41-15168:8": -2.4821906089782715,
            "clueweb22-en0028-24-06992:1": -2.824375867843628,
            "clueweb22-en0022-21-18497:7": -2.8980116844177246
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": []
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 4,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Perfect, that clears things up. Could you list a few shampoos with salicylic acid that work for oily scalps? I also use heat styling tools, so lightweight and non-stripping would be ideal.",
          "user_rubrik": "What shampoos exist for an oily scalp and hair?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "here are salicylic - acid shampoos that suit oily scalps and won \u2019 t feel heavy. i \u2019 ve avoided argan, shea, macadamia, and almond oils for your nut allergy. - neutrogena t / sal therapeutic shampoo ( 3 % salicylic acid ) : excellent for oily scalp and buildup. use 2 \u2013 3x / week ; leave on scalp 2 \u2013 3 minutes, then rinse. lightweight and non - waxy. - kenkoderm psoriasis shampoo ( salicylic acid + panthenol ) : helps clear oil / flakes and buildup while staying light. double - check the inci to confirm no nut - derived oils. helpful pairings ( non \u2013 salicylic acid ) for in - between washes : - neutrogena anti - residue shampoo : once weekly as a clarifying \u201c reset. \u201d - maple holistics degrease or tea tree sulfate - free shampoo : gentle daily / every - other - day options without nut oils. use tips for less stripping with heat styling : - cleanse scalp only ; condition mid - lengths / ends with a light, silicone",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0012-98-11457:2": -2.488602638244629,
            "clueweb22-en0042-31-02488:2": -2.686004161834717,
