      {
        "turn": 5,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Thanks, I\u2019ll check them out! Can you tell me more about OUAI and Head & Shoulders for oily scalp and hair\u2014are they good options?",
          "user_rubrik": "Tell me more about OUAI and Head and Shoulders brands for shampoo for oily scalp and hair.\u00a0",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Short answer: yes\u2014both can work for oily scalps, used the right way.  - OUAI Detox Shampoo: Strong clarifying wash that removes oil, product, and hard\u2011water buildup\u2014great if you use heat protectants and stylers. Use 1x/week (2x if very oily); it can feel drying if used daily. Focus on scalp, then lightly condition mid\u2011lengths/ends. Typically free of nut oils, but always check the label.  - Head & Shoulders: Good everyday option for oily/itchy or flaky scalps thanks to zinc pyrithione. Choose Itchy Scalp Care (eucalyptus) or Classic Clean; they\u2019re lighter and generally non\u2011stripping. Massage in and leave on scalp 1\u20132 minutes before rinsing. Avoid the \u201cSupreme\u201d line (often includes argan oil), given your nut allergy.  How to pair: - Use Head & Shoulders daily or every other day. - Use OUAI Detox as your weekly reset to cut buildup from styling and hard water.  Tip: If anything feels tight or irritated, reduce frequency and switch to a gentler, pH\u2011balanced shampoo on off days.",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0011-48-08853:0": 0.022790536284446716,
