    "responses": [
      {
        "turn": 1,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Hi! I was wondering, what\u2019s a good shampoo to use if I have an oily scalp and hair?",
          "user_rubrik": "What is a good shampoo for my hair?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "For an oily scalp, choose a clarifying but gentle shampoo that controls sebum without over\u2011stripping. Look for formulas with ingredients like tea tree, peppermint, lemon, rosemary, ginger or basil \u2014 they help reduce oil and refresh the scalp. Good options to consider: a mild clarifying/degrease shampoo (botanical blends), pH\u2011balanced scalp\u2011balancing shampoos, or targeted oily\u2011scalp anti\u2011dandruff/anti\u2011sebum formulas.  Practical tips: - Wash every day or every other day as needed; don\u2019t pile conditioner on the roots \u2014 apply only to mid\u2011lengths and ends.   - Use a sulfate\u2011free clarifying product if your hair is color\u2011treated or you want less drying; a stronger clarifier can be used once weekly to remove buildup.   - If you also have thinning/hair\u2011loss concerns, choose an oily\u2011scalp formula that includes strengthening botanicals or keratin.  If you want, tell me your hair type (fine/thick, color\u2011treated, any sensitivity) and I\u2019ll recommend specific bottles.",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0004-84-05824:5": 34.52399826049805,
            "clueweb22-en0001-78-15977:0": 33.97489929199219,
            "clueweb22-en0016-13-03599:4": 33.51890182495117,
            "clueweb22-en0010-88-09918:2": 33.37030029296875,
            "clueweb22-en0041-44-13888:3": 33.126399993896484
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": []
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 2,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "What about specific ingredients I should avoid in shampoo, especially if I use heat tools a lot and have an oily scalp?",
          "user_rubrik": "What ingredients in the shampoo i should look out for?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Good question \u2014 for an oily scalp that\u2019s heat\u2011styled often, avoid ingredients that either strip and dry the scalp (which can trigger more oil) or build up and weigh roots down.  Ingredients to avoid - Sulfates (SLS, SLES): very stripping and can overstimulate oil production.   - High\u2011content drying alcohols (denat., SD alcohols): dry hair and make heat damage worse.   - Heavy oils/waxes and thick emollients (petrolatum, heavy mineral oils, waxes): cause buildup on oily scalps.   - Heavy, non\u2011water\u2011soluble silicones (dimethicone, amodimethicone when used near roots): can accumulate and make hair greasy.   - Excessive fragrance or harsh chemical formulas if you have sensitivity.  Practical tips - Use a gentle clarifying or degrease shampoo (sulfate\u2011free if color\u2011treated) and reserve stronger clarifiers for weekly use.   - Don\u2019t put conditioner on the scalp; apply mid\u2011lengths to ends only.   - Always use a good heat\u2011protectant before styling.",
          "citations": {
