          "user_rubrik": "What shampoos exist for an oily scalp and hair?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "yes \u2014 la roche - posay does make a hair line and their kerium ds anti \u2011 dandruff intensive shampoo is a good salon \u2011 grade pick if your oily scalp also has heavy dandruff or itching. it uses micro \u2011 exfoliating lha and anti \u2011 itching niacinamide ( vitamin pp ) to remove flakes and treat the scalp root. if you just want a gentler, daily degreasing shampoo ( sulfate \u2011 free option ) look at botanical \u201c degrease \u201d formulas \u2014 they often include rosemary, lemon, basil, jojoba or keratin to balance sebum without over \u2011 stripping. maple holistics degrease shampoo is an example favored for oily, itchy scalps and is sulfate \u2011 free. caution : some anti \u2011 dandruff or very harsh clarifying shampoos ( and some head & shoulders users report ) can overstimulate sebum production ; if that happens switch to a gentler formula and give your scalp 1 \u2013 2 weeks to rebalance. if you want, tell me if you have dandruff, sensitivity, color \u2011 treated hair or thinning and i \u2019 ll recommend",
