        "turn": 1,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Hi! I was wondering, what\u2019s a good shampoo to use if I have an oily scalp and hair?",
          "user_rubrik": "What is a good shampoo for my hair?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "For an oily scalp, choose a clarifying but gentle shampoo that controls sebum without over\u2011stripping. Look for formulas with ingredients like tea tree, peppermint, lemon, rosemary, ginger or basil \u2014 they help reduce oil and refresh the scalp. Good options to consider: a mild clarifying/degrease shampoo (botanical blends), pH\u2011balanced scalp\u2011balancing shampoos, or targeted oily\u2011scalp anti\u2011dandruff/anti\u2011sebum formulas.  Practical tips: - Wash every day or every other day as needed; don\u2019t pile conditioner on the roots \u2014 apply only to mid\u2011lengths and ends.   - Use a sulfate\u2011free clarifying product if your hair is color\u2011treated or you want less drying; a stronger clarifier can be used once weekly to remove buildup.   - If you also have thinning/hair\u2011loss concerns, choose an oily\u2011scalp formula that includes strengthening botanicals or keratin.  If you want, tell me your hair type (fine/thick, color\u2011treated, any sensitivity) and I\u2019ll recommend specific bottles.",
