          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "I\u2019m curious about finding a good shampoo\u2014what kind should I look for?",
          "user_rubrik": "What is a good shampoo for my hair?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "great question \u2014 pick a shampoo based on your hair condition and styling habits. quick guide : - if you heat - style often : choose a gentle, moisturizing / repairing shampoo with proteins ( keratin or hydrolyzed amino acids ) and panthenol ( b5 ) to help strengthen and retain moisture. follow with a heat \u2011 protectant leave \u2011 in. - if hair feels dry or frizzy : look for hydrating formulas ( aloe, jojoba, hyaluronic acid ) and weekly nourishing masks. - if hair is fine or thinning : try a volumizing / thickening shampoo with botanical stimulants ( ginseng - type extracts ) and amino - acid blends. - if you color hair : pick a sulfate - free, uv \u2011 protective shampoo to preserve color. - scalp concerns : use a mild, microbiome - friendly or anti \u2011 flaky formula if you have flaking or oiliness. - allergy note : because you \u2019 re nut \u2011 allergic, scan labels for nut - derived ingredients ( almond, shea, macadamia, argan, etc. ) and patch - test new products. also use a lightweight",
