          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "good question \u2014 short list of ingredients to avoid if you have an oily scalp ( and a nut allergy ) : - heavy oils / butters that can weigh hair and clog pores : argan, macadamia, shea, coconut, olive, avocado. ( skip nut \u2011 derived oils entirely given your allergy. ) - non \u2011 water \u2011 soluble silicones that cause buildup and limpness : dimethicone, amodimethicone. ( water \u2011 soluble silicones are gentler. ) - heavy emollients / waxes and mineral oils : petrolatum, mineral oil, paraffin, beeswax \u2014 they can leave residue. - harsh surfactants and stripping detergents : sodium lauryl sulfate ( sls ) and similar strong sulfates \u2014 they can over \u2011 strip and trigger rebound oiliness and flaking. - high amounts of conditioning quats or thick cationic agents ( in leave \u2011 ins or conditioners ) that can sit at the roots. - fragrance and known irritants if you notice scalp sensitivity. prefer lightweight, clarifying formulas with gentle surfactants, salicylic acid, clay or tea \u2011 tree extracts, and rinse \u2011 out",
