          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That\u2019s great, thanks! What about well-known brands like OUAI or Head & Shoulders\u2014are their shampoos good for oily scalps?",
          "user_rubrik": "Tell me more about OUAI and Head and Shoulders brands for shampoo for oily scalp and hair.\u00a0",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Both can work \u2014 but they serve different roles.  - OUAI Detox: a clarifying/detox shampoo designed to remove oil, product and hard\u2011water buildup. Good as a weekly or occasional deep clean if your hair gets weighed down or you use lots of styling products. Don\u2019t use it every day if your hair is already dry from heat styling.  - Head & Shoulders: aimed at dandruff/oily scalps (zinc pyrithione formulas) and has oil\u2011control and charcoal variants. Good for regular use if you have flaking or persistent oiliness \u2014 it treats the scalp rather than just stripping residue.  Tips for you (oily scalp + nut allergy): - Rotate: a gentle daily clarifying or tea\u2011tree/salicylic shampoo + OUAI detox once a week. - If you have dandruff/itching, favor Head & Shoulders or a medicated anti\u2011dandruff option. - Always read labels for nut\u2011derived oils (argan, macadamia, shea, etc.), sulfates or heavy silicones, and patch\u2011test new products.",
